DURAK PROJECT MANAGER / ENGINEERING REPORT

Durak
Project Audit
& Roadmap

20 October 2026

Current status

The existing React / Colyseus / shared-rules monorepo has a substantial working gameplay core. A playable Three.js table
and multiplayer integrity tranche are implemented. Further polish and public-release validation remain.
Baseline: 218 tests passed; four lint warnings; ten server type errors; root production build failed.
Current checks: 297 tests pass, all workspace type checks pass, client lint is clean and the root build succeeds. The client
bundle-size warning remains.
Implemented: private network state, verified room identities, lobby guards, a real 3D table, complete bot and two-client
browser matches, rematch/refresh recovery and WebGL fallback. Custom shared engine rules are retained.
Next release blockers: four high dependency advisories remain after compatible updates removed all critical findings.
Physical-device performance, production persistence, Redis, external Discord integration and deployment need validation.

Report contents

1. Full project audit — architecture, baseline checks, prioritized findings and custom rules.
2. Implementation roadmap — milestones, acceptance criteria and first-tranche results.

Source of record: docs/PROJECT_AUDIT.md and docs/PROJECT_PLAN.md. The audit describes the original baseline; the
roadmap records subsequent fixes. Local browser smoke checks passed; no deployment or complete production
acceptance run has been performed.

DURAK / Technical audit & implementation roadmap / 20 Oct 2026                                                                1
Durak project audit

Owner: Durak Project Manager. Inspected 2026-10-20 at commit 9b23e50. This records the unmodified baseline;
implementation results appear in PROJECT_PLAN.md.

Architecture and working behavior

This is an npm workspace monorepo, not a Three.js application yet.

Client

packages/client/src/main.tsx, App.tsx; React 19, Vite 8, Tailwind, Framer Motion. contexts/GameContext.tsx owns
Colyseus connections, patch-driven rerenders, reconnect tokens, broadcasts and matchmaking. AuthContext.tsx handles
browser identity.
Evidence and limits: 88 component tests pass. Active play uses components/GameBoard.tsx; home uses HomePage.tsx. No
Three.js dependency or scene exists.

Server

packages/server/index.ts: Express APIs, OAuth/JWT, profiles/shop/history, optional Redis, static client hosting.
src/rooms/DurakRoom.ts: lobby, dealing, Suhuh, action validation, clockwise progression, timeout, bots, reconnect,
spectators, results/rematch and persistence.
Evidence and limits: 64 tests pass, including a real Colyseus client/server action sequence. Most room tests call private
handlers directly; these do not prove browser flows or deployment.

Shared

packages/shared/index.ts exports schemas, engine, badges and ladder. src/state/* is the network schema;
src/engine/DurakEngine.ts supplies comparisons, mass composition, defense matching, drawing, pickup and Huzur
exchange.
Evidence and limits: 66 tests pass across 16 files: custom modes, conservation, stacking, swaps, tiers. Engine helpers
mutate state; the architecture description calling everything stateless is inaccurate.

Bots

packages/server/src/ai/BotEngine.ts is imported and executed by the room. Easy/hard bots evaluate actual moves.
Evidence and limits: Shared src/ai/GrandmasterBot.ts, MCTS.ts, InferenceEngine.ts form a separate, unconnected
prototype. Grandmaster only returns pickup; MCTS scores random coin flips.

Deployment

Root Dockerfile and packages/server/Dockerfile build client assets and run server TypeScript through ts-node.
.github/workflows/ci.yml runs checks and Fly deployment. Capacitor native projects are present.
Evidence and limits: External MongoDB, Redis, Discord, Fly and native builds were not exercised. Docker does not
compile and run a plain-JS server as README claims.

