Prioritized findings

P0 = blocks public competitive release; P1 = blocks reliable development or target functionality; P2 = maintainability /
polish.

P0 / Hidden information is serialized publicly: shared/src/state/Player.ts exposes hand, lastDrawLog,
pickedUpCardKeys; GameState.ts exposes full ordered deck and actionLog.
server/src/rooms/DurakRoom.ts::logPendingDraws puts exact draws into that log. CSS card backs
cannot protect these values.

Action: Design owner-only hands, public hand/deck counts and server-only deck/replay data; test decoded snapshots
and patches for two players plus spectator and reconnect. Audit broadcasts as well as schema fields.

P0 / DurakRoom.ts::onAuth validates room eligibility, not identity. onJoin accepts arbitrary userId /
discordId from options; saveGameLog uses them for profiles/rating/rewards. API JWT verification
does not secure room joins.

Action: Verify server-issued tokens at join; derive profile identities from verified claims; keep explicit guests unrated. Test
impersonation rejection.

DURAK / Technical audit & implementation roadmap / 20 Oct 2026                                                                   3
P0 / DurakRoom.ts::onCreate registers production-accessible dev_action: host can play_as another
player or force_pass; arbitrary testModeDeck is accepted at creation.

Action: Deny debug mutation and deck injection in production while retaining legitimate lobby bot setup. Add
handler-level regression tests.

P1 / Root build fails; server type errors and missing server CI validation (see baseline).
Source-based server runtime is intentional today.

Action: Establish reliable workspace build/typecheck commands and exercise them in CI; describe runtime accurately.

P1 / No Three.js renderer. client/src/components/GameBoard.tsx mixes lobby, scene layout, drag
staging, developer controls, results and audio in ~2,700 lines.

Action: Extract reusable action/presentation adapters; add a lazy-loaded scene without duplicating rules or connection
ownership. Preserve a functional accessible DOM path.

P1 / Solo UI in HomePage.tsx::SinglePlayerSheet sends botDifficulty, ignored by the baseline room,
and handSize: 6. The UI advertises medium difficulty, but server/src/ai/BotEngine.ts only
implements easy/hard.

Action: Wire solo creation to real bots, use a documented hand size, and expose only supported difficulties. Verify the
actual room join/start path.

P1 / Room options are weakly validated in DurakRoom.ts::onCreate / updateSettings: raw parseInt for
capacity/hand size, arbitrary mode strings, client-controlled test fixtures. Several handlers
assume non-null payloads.

Action: Centralize supported combinations and payload validation; ensure malformed traffic cannot crash handlers or
create invalid games.

P1 / Rule/documentation divergence: GAME_RULES.md calls this single-player despite existing
multiplayer; Suhuh specifies a separate deck and team choice, while DurakRoom.ts::resolveSuhuh
draws/returns actual undealt cards and resolves automatically. Engine initializeGame deals
round-robin with shift and chooses player zero; production room deals a whole hand per
player with pop, then Suhuh. GAME_NOTATION.md still mentions six-card refills and nonexistent
sixes.

Action: Preserve current behavior pending explicit rule decisions; characterize differences in tests, then converge setup
paths. Do not silently substitute standard Durak.

P1 / server/index.ts exposes /colyseus monitor without access control. Broad CORS/frame
policy, identity APIs, proxy and production config need a deployment review.

Action: Protect/disable monitor in production and test the actual deployment configuration before public launch.

P2 / Four hook warnings in GameBoard.tsx and PlayerProfilePanel.tsx. Profile fetch depends only
on discordId despite reading email userId; it can show stale content.

Action: Capture primitive effect inputs, use explicit dependencies and verify existing tests.

