Tranche 0 results

Completed locally:

• Root npm run typecheck checks all three workspaces, including client project references and server tests. Server/shared
    build performs no-emit validation because deployment still uses source through ts-node; the client emits production
    assets.

• CI now uses Node 24 (matching the audited local major), checks server types and builds all workspaces. CI itself and
    containers were not executed locally.

• Production host debug impersonation/force-pass/dummies are blocked. Real easy/hard bots remain available in
    waiting lobbies. Client deck injection is restricted to test environments.

• Solo room options now provision a registered bot and start the match after the human joins. Unsupported
    configurations are rejected; the client requests five cards and offers the two implemented difficulties. Artwork is
    retained.

• Timer/result/staging effects use explicit primitive dependencies. Profile panel refetches when either email or Discord
    identity changes. Historical docs point to the verified audit/plan.

